Ratelimit the map-failure error message.

Backport of upstream v6 patch 11 ("nvme-rdma: ratelimit the map-failure
error message"). A mapping failure is per-request and, for an
unroutable P2P transfer, deterministic: a workload that keeps issuing
one turns this into a log line per I/O. Ratelimit it, as nvme's
per-I/O error logging (nvme_log_error()) already is.

Applies to the rhel10 vendored rdma.c (after 0001 and any earlier
patches in this series). Applied by bin/build-nvme-tarball: patch -p1
--fuzz=0 -d <variant dir>.
Regeneration after re-vendoring: dkms-nvme/README.md, 'Refreshing'.

--- a/rdma.c
+++ b/rdma.c
@@ -2039,8 +2039,8 @@
 
 	err = nvme_rdma_map_data(queue, rq, c);
 	if (unlikely(err < 0)) {
-		dev_err(queue->ctrl->ctrl.device,
-			     "Failed to map data (%d)\n", err);
+		dev_err_ratelimited(queue->ctrl->ctrl.device,
+				    "Failed to map data (%d)\n", err);
 		goto err;
 	}
 
